    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAs in the title.\n\nFor context, this `E:2` can be shown by LSP. Although this part isn't LSP-specific. See https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/runtime/lua/vim/diagnostic.lua#L1107 .\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nLooks like this config can solve the problem, though it copies a lot of code from the file above.\n\n```lua\nlocal severity = vim.diagnostic.severity\n\n-- Copied from neovim/runtime/lua/vim/diagnostic.lua\nlocal hl_map = {\n  [severity.ERROR] = 'DiagnosticSignError',\n  [severity.WARN] = 'DiagnosticSignWarn',\n  [severity.INFO] = 'DiagnosticSignInfo',\n  [severity.HINT] = 'DiagnosticSignHint',\n}\nlocal default_status_signs = {\n  [severity.ERROR] = 'E',\n  [severity.WARN] = 'W',\n  [severity.INFO] = 'I',\n  [severity.HINT] = 'H',\n}\n\n_G.OpenDiagnosticQuickfix = function(severity)\n  local winid = vim.fn.getmousepos().winid\n  if winid == 0 then\n    return\n  end\n  local bufnr = vim.api.nvim_win_get_buf(winid)\n  local diagnostics = vim.diagnostic.get(bufnr, { severity = severity })\n  vim.fn.setqflist({}, ' ', {\n    items = vim.diagnostic.toqflist(diagnostics),\n  })\n  vim.cmd('copen')\nend\n\nvim.diagnostic.config({\n  status = {\n    format = function(counts)\n      local signs_config = vim.diagnostic.config().signs\n      local signs = type(signs_config) == 'table' and signs_config.text or default_status_signs\n\n      return vim.iter(pairs(counts))\n        :map(function(severity, count)\n          return ('%%%d@v:lua.OpenDiagnosticQuickfix@%%#%s#%s:%s%%T'):format(\n            severity, hl_map[severity], signs[severity], count\n          )\n        end)\n        :join(' ')\n    end,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe function `vim.diagnostic.setqflist` can also be used, but it doesn't have per-buffer filtering (the local function `set_list` is used, but it explicitly only assign `bufnr` in the `loclist` branch)",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've long wanted to add a lot more discoverability via mouse-clicks in 'statusline'. It's rather fresh territory. The features are mostly there, just haven't been exploited yet. \n\nAnd it can be done in a way that is zero-cost for users that don't use the mouse.",
